<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Meidum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Meidum is an archaeological site in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> on the desert edge west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nile">Nile</a>, about 100 km south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cairo">Cairo</a>. Its pyramid, completed under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sneferu">Sneferu</a> in the 26th century BCE, was converted from a step pyramid into a true pyramid and later lost much of its outer casing. Nearby mastaba tombs yielded the painted Meidum Geese and the statues of Rahotep and Nofret.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/meidum.jpg" alt="Meidum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kurohito · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Meidoum03.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
